[size=5][b]psi_autocast_mfd: an in-game psi macro MFD[/b][/size]

Plan your psionics and build [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/systemshock225thanniversaryremaster/mods/20]psi-autocast[/url] macros without leaving the game. Press one key, and an MFD in the game's own teal style opens over the view.

[b]A restart is the most you'll ever have to do: no manual edits, if you don't want them.[/b]

[line]
[size=4][b]What it shows[/b][/size]
A scrolling table of all 35 disciplines, each with its icon, tier and name, and:
[list]
[*][b]Duration[/b] at your current PSI and at PSI 8.[/*]
[*][b]Effect[/b] at your current PSI and at PSI 8: damage, healing, stat bonus, chance or recharge, whichever the discipline has.[/*]
[*][b]Overload[/b]: what an overload gives you, for the disciplines that benefit from one.[/*]
[*][b]Cyber Mods[/b]: "bought", or what it costs, including every tier you still need to unlock to reach it.[/*]
[/list]
The numbers are read from the running game, so they follow SCP if you use it. Cyber module costs follow your difficulty, rounded the way the game rounds them.

[line]
[size=4][b]Building macros[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Pick a key with the [b]<[/b] [b]>[/b] arrows, or click [b]Keys[/b] (or the key name) to choose it from a keyboard.[/*]
[*]Click a discipline, or its [b]+Overload[/b] / [b]+Quick[/b] button, to add a cast.[/*]
[*]Add psi hypos, change the waits between steps, and finish with a switch back to your previous weapon or to any weapon.[/*]
[*]Options: draw the psi amp first, how long to wait for it, and auto psi hypo.[/*]
[*][b]Save[/b], close the MFD, and press the key. psi_autocast runs the macro.[/*]
[/list]
Scroll the table with the Up / Dn buttons, or jump to a tier with T1-T5. With the optional wheel lines (below), the mouse wheel scrolls it too when the cursor is over the MFD, and still switches weapons everywhere else.

[line]
[size=4][b]The keyboard[/b][/size]
[b]Keys[/b] swaps the table for a keyboard. Hover a key to see what it does; click one to pick it.
[list]
[*][b]Bright teal[/b]: a macro key. A double outline means it has a saved macro (or runs a psi_autocast script).[/*]
[*][b]Teal[/b]: free, no binding yet.[/*]
[*][b]Grey[/b]: set by the game in Options > Controls.[/*]
[*][b]Blue-grey[/b]: used by these mods (the MFD's open key, keypad + for psi_autocast's cancel).[/*]
[*][b]Dim[/b]: never used for macros (Enter, Esc, Tab, Space, Backspace, Shift, Ctrl, Alt, ` - =).[/*]
[/list]
Marks: [b]=[/b] the key's job is also on another key; red [b]![/b] it has a saved macro but is still set to something else; [b]?[/b] its macro file has no steps.
Letters, digits, F-keys, the navigation keys (i.e. home, ins, end), keypad numbers, arrows, and the comma, period, slash, semicolon, apostrophe, bracket and backslash keys can all hold macros.

[line]
[size=4][b]Setup[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install and enable [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/systemshock225thanniversaryremaster/mods/20]psi_autocast[/url] 1.2 or later.[/*]
[*]Extract this mod into the [b]game folder[/b], the one with [b]SystemShock2Remastered.exe[/b] (not the save folder). It adds [i]mods\psi_autocast_mfd.kpf[/i].[/*]
[*]New Game → Mods → add [b]psi_autocast_mfd[/b] (keep psi_autocast) → Apply → start, then load your save and make a regular save.[/*]
[*]On that first load, the MFD binds keypad * to open it (or the next free key), and keypad + to psi_autocast's cancel if that's free. Restart the game once when it tells you to, then press keypad *.[/*]
[*][b]In a new game, wait until you're through training before using the MFD:[/b] macros don't take before then.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Keys[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Saving on a free key[/b] binds it for you: "Saved. Restart the game for O to run this macro."[/*]
[*][b]Saving on a key the game uses[/b]: clear it in Options > Controls first, then Save again and restart. The MFD never takes a key away from the game's own controls.[/*]
[*][b]Saving on a macro key[/b] works on the next keypress.[/*]
[/list]
The game reads key bindings only when it starts, which is why a new key needs one restart. Before the MFD changes [i]user.bnd[/i], it backs it up as [i]user.bnd.mfd_backup[/i].

If you'd rather set keys up yourself, you still can:

Setup Script (GitHub only):
[spoiler][size=4][b]The setup script[/b][/size]
[url=https://github.com/feygon/SS2PsiAutocastMFD/releases/latest]setupPsiMfd.bat[/url], from the GitHub release, writes the [i]user.bnd[/i] lines for many keys at once. Run it with the game closed. It:
[list]
[*]binds an open key to the MFD: default keypad *, or another free key;[/*]
[*]binds keypad + to psi_autocast's cancel key, if it's free;[/*]
[*]gives G and J psi_autocast's two starter casts, as macros you can edit (it also takes over the starter keys from psi_autocast's own starter script);[/*]
[*]binds a macro key on every plain key you haven't bound: letters, digits, F-keys, keypad and navigation keys (i.e. home, ins, end), keypad numbers, arrows and punctuation;[/*]
[*]asks you, one key at a time (y/n), about a key you've already bound only if the game doesn't bind it by default and its command is also on another key, so saying yes never loses a command; it changes no other binding;[/*]
[*]never uses Enter, Esc, Tab, Space, Backspace, modifier keys, or ` - =;[/*]
[*]asks (y/n) whether the mouse wheel should scroll the MFD, only while the wheel has the game's default bindings or none;[/*]
[*]backs up [i]user.bnd[/i] first, lists every key it bound, and adds only what's missing if you run it again.[/*]
[/list]
[/spoiler]

Manual Setup:
[spoiler][size=4][b]The user.bnd lines[/b][/size]
[i]user.bnd[/i] is in [i]%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\Nightdive Studios\System Shock 2 Remastered\[/i]. Back it up, then edit it with the game closed.

One key opens and closes the MFD:
[code]bind keypad_star "summon_obj PsiMfd"[/code]
Each macro key runs its own file. Add one line per key you want, changing the key and the file name together:
[code]bind keypad_minus "run user:/psi_macros\Macro_keypad_minus.cmd"
bind keypad_del "run user:/psi_macros\Macro_keypad_del.cmd"[/code]
The MFD finds your macro keys by reading these lines, so every key you add this way appears in its selector.

Optional: the mouse wheel scrolls the MFD when the cursor is over it, and switches weapons everywhere else. Replace the two [i]mouse_wheel[/i] lines with:
[code]bind mouse_wheel_up "summon_obj PsiMfdWheelUp"
bind mouse_wheel_down "summon_obj PsiMfdWheelDown"[/code]
In a save without psi_autocast_mfd enabled, the wheel then doesn't switch weapons. To undo, put back [i]bind mouse_wheel_up "cycle_weapon 1"[/i] and [i]bind mouse_wheel_down "cycle_weapon -1"[/i].[/spoiler]

[line]
[size=4][b]What it writes[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Macros[/b]: small text files in [i]Saved Games\Nightdive Studios\System Shock 2 Remastered\psi_macros\[/i], one per key, in the same format the psi_autocast Macro Builder writes.[/*]
[*][b]Key bindings[/b]: [i]user.bnd[/i], only when you save on a free key or on the first load without an open key, backed up first as [i]user.bnd.mfd_backup[/i].[/*]
[/list]
It doesn't touch the game folder.

The mod itself is five text files: no images, nothing downloaded. The discipline icons and the MFD's background are the remaster's own art, loaded from the game at runtime.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]System Shock 2: 25th Anniversary Remaster on PC. Tested on the Epic version, game version 1.3.4984.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/systemshock225thanniversaryremaster/mods/20]psi_autocast[/url], enabled alongside it.[/*]
[*]Tested alongside the remaster's bundled mods (SCP beta 6, SHTUP, Four Hundred, patch_ext). Multiplayer is untested.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Source and license[/b][/size]
